WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:06.060
Multiversal epics, street-level thrillers,&nbsp;
and even a sitcom or two — Phase 4 of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:10.535
the MCU really had it all. But which&nbsp;
projects soared… and which ones sank?

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:15.720
The MCU's first half-hour sitcom, She-Hulk:&nbsp;
Attorney at Law is, as Jennifer Walters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:20.640
repeatedly insists, a lawyer show — except when&nbsp;
a rampaging antagonist forces Jen to Hulk out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:25.200
and smash stuff. The show recounts She-Hulk's&nbsp;
origin story and explains how she reluctantly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:30.000
becomes a part-time superhero. Plus, Jen's&nbsp;
new She-Hulk status opens the door for all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.760
kinds of MCU cameos, and nearly every episode&nbsp;
includes at least one big-name guest star.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:40.800
"I know you can't wait to see Wong. I get&nbsp;
it. I just wanna make sure that you don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:44.280
think that this is one of those 'cameo&nbsp;
every week' type of shows. It's not."

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:50.400
All of this proves to be a lot of laugh-out-loud&nbsp;
fun, but it also makes for a wildly uneven nine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:54.780
episodes, where the show's penchant for&nbsp;
meta-comedy and mocking MCU tropes often&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:59.280
come at the expense of the story. Still, critics&nbsp;
and audiences were polarized over whether that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:04.260
was a good thing or a bad thing. On the one hand,&nbsp;
critics mostly praised the series, appreciating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:09.600
what made it funny and enjoyable over its flaws.&nbsp;
However, common fan criticisms included the show's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:14.130
weak plotting, the CGI, and the comedy, which&nbsp;
some found to be more cringey than chuckle-worthy.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:16.860
Out of all the films in the franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:21.780
Eternals feels the least like an MCU film. The&nbsp;
story of a group of 10 immortal superpowered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:26.400
aliens who came to Earth millennia ago to protect&nbsp;
the world against the destructive Deviants,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:30.900
Eternals sees the titular heroes reuniting&nbsp;
after a Deviant emerges in modern-day London.

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:34.800
With so many new characters and a&nbsp;
story spanning thousands of years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:39.300
Eternals was always going to be an odd&nbsp;
fit within the greater MCU. The movie is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:44.280
undeniably ambitious, and Oscar-winning director&nbsp;
Chloé Zhao ensures it features stunning visuals,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:49.800
absorbing exposition, and a calmer, quieter&nbsp;
tone than many of its more frantic counterparts.

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:52.800
But critics complained that&nbsp;
the film is also overly long&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:56.880
and burdened with uninspired action&nbsp;
sequences, unoriginal plot points,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:02.160
and a chemistry-free central romance between&nbsp;
Gemma Chan's Sersi and Richard Madden's Ikaris.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:06.300
Eternals does introduce some intriguing&nbsp;
new elements into the MCU, but on balance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:10.298
it never quite captures the imagination&nbsp;
like the franchise's other entries.

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:15.780
Thor: Love and Thunder is a fun and buoyant&nbsp;
addition to a universe that has begun to feel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:20.100
a little weighed down by its attempts to forge&nbsp;
new directions in the wake of the Infinity Saga.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:23.940
Yet many critics have complained that Love&nbsp;
and Thunder feels like a less innovative&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:29.400
redo of 2017's Thor: Ragnarok, making for a&nbsp;
film that's locked too much in its own past.

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:33.000
The movie's story picks up with Thor&nbsp;
still traveling the universe with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:37.200
Guardians of the Galaxy following the events&nbsp;
of Avengers: Endgame. Everything changes when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:41.580
he returns to New Asgard to discover his&nbsp;
ex-girlfriend Jane Foster fighting as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:47.220
Mighty Thor against a new threat, Gorr the God&nbsp;
Butcher, who is intent on eradicating the gods.

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:54.334
"This is my vow. All gods will die."

00:02:54.334 --> 00:02:58.560
Love and Thunder is a vibrant journey through&nbsp;
space accompanied by plenty of humor, heart,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:03.120
and even a touch of horror, all set to a&nbsp;
rollicking metal soundtrack. Yet while the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:08.220
movie offers plenty for long-time MCU fans to&nbsp;
love, for some, the story may feel a little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:12.360
redundant or disjointed. For others, it&nbsp;
may even seem like a step back for Thor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:17.134
a character who has been through a lot but&nbsp;
doesn't seem to have grown all that much.

00:03:17.134 --> 00:03:21.780
There was plenty of excitement when it was&nbsp;
announced that Sam Raimi, director of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:25.800
original Spider-Man trilogy, would helm the&nbsp;
second movie in the Doctor Strange series.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:31.620
Fans were eager to see how a superhero veteran&nbsp;
like Raimi would handle an MCU film. Perhaps the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:35.160
most interesting thing about Raimi's approach&nbsp;
to Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of Madness,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:39.300
however, is that his style appears more&nbsp;
in the movie's horror beats, which often&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:44.220
recall Raimi's Evil Dead movies. Moreover,&nbsp;
while this is a Doctor Strange movie, it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:49.320
as much about Elizabeth Olsen's grieving Wanda&nbsp;
Maximoff as it is the one-time Sorcerer Supreme.

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:54.600
The story finds Strange and Wong rescuing America&nbsp;
Chavez, a girl with the ability to hop across the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:59.100
multiverse. Chavez is being pursued by&nbsp;
Wanda, leading to an epic chase across&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:04.560
universes. Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of&nbsp;
Madness is a distinctly dark entry in the MCU,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:09.120
which makes it stand out from the lighter tone&nbsp;
of many of its predecessors. For this one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:13.320
though, fans' and critics' mileage will&nbsp;
vary depending on how much they buy into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:17.552
Wanda's story — as well as how much&nbsp;
they enjoy the movie's scarier side.

00:04:17.552 --> 00:04:22.320
When Chris Evans' Captain America departed the&nbsp;
MCU at the end of Avengers: Endgame, he left a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:27.720
void at the heart of the franchise that fans knew&nbsp;
would have to be filled. The six-part Disney+&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:32.340
series The Falcon and the Winter Soldier was&nbsp;
created to illustrate exactly how that happens.

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:40.740
"We built this country. Bled for it. I'm not&nbsp;
gonna let anyone tell me I can't fight for it."

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:46.380
The show also tackles the rise of the&nbsp;
U.S.-sanctioned Captain America, John Walker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:51.780
as well as the threat posed by the supersoldier&nbsp;
Flag Smashers and the dastardly Helmut Zemo.

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:56.280
Although the series starts slow, once it&nbsp;
takes off, critics found that it packs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.280 --> 00:05:00.420
in plenty of heart-pumping action, some&nbsp;
timely political and social commentary,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:06.060
and a hugely enjoyable dynamic between Sam and&nbsp;
Bucky. The show is a little unfocused at times,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:10.706
sure, but it's still a rewarding insight into&nbsp;
these two less well-known MCU characters.

00:05:10.706 --> 00:05:16.500
After a lengthy delay due to the pandemic, Black&nbsp;
Widow was the first movie to finally be released&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:21.060
as part of Phase 4. The film sheds light on the&nbsp;
backstory of Natasha Romanoff, a character who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:26.160
entered the MCU back in 2010 with Iron Man 2.&nbsp;
Yet because it's a movie about a character who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:31.560
died in Avengers: Endgame and takes place between&nbsp;
Civil War and Infinity War, the movie feels like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:35.880
more of an afterthought than it might have had it&nbsp;
been made and released earlier in the franchise.

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:40.800
Still, Natasha finally gets the solo movie she&nbsp;
always deserved, and her story leads to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:45.420
introduction of several exciting new characters.&nbsp;
Moreover, critics found the film funny, touching,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:49.800
and relatable. Some noted that it casts&nbsp;
Natasha in the spotlight she always deserved,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:54.000
placing her in a pleasingly standalone&nbsp;
adventure unlike anything we've seen her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:58.980
in before. Unfortunately, the film's rote action&nbsp;
and underwhelming villains pull much of the focus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.980 --> 00:06:04.088
making for an entertaining but uneven&nbsp;
swan song for one of the O.G. Avengers.

00:06:04.088 --> 00:06:09.300
By the time Moon Knight was released, magic&nbsp;
was an established part of the MCU, but it had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:14.280
never been used quite like it is in this series.&nbsp;
This Disney+ series is the tale of Marc Spector,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:18.480
a mercenary who is also the avatar for the&nbsp;
Egyptian god Khonshu. Marc's life would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:23.580
complicated enough if doing the deity's bidding&nbsp;
was the only thing he had to worry about. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:27.840
Marc also has Dissociative Identity&nbsp;
Disorder, and when one of his alters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:31.980
Steven Grant, discovers what he's&nbsp;
been up to, things get even dicier.

00:06:31.980 --> 00:06:35.580
With its deep dive into Egyptian&nbsp;
mythology, superhero antics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:41.100
and multiple main characters sharing one body,&nbsp;
Moon Knight is a decidedly unusual MCU outing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:45.720
The show's mythology-driven plot gets awfully&nbsp;
technical at times, and that combined with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:49.920
some ho-hum action sequences can lead to&nbsp;
a few lulls in the story. Overall, though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:54.480
critics praised Moon Knight for being absorbing&nbsp;
and entertaining, especially as it dives deeper&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:59.700
into Marc's backstory — and it's all anchored by&nbsp;
an impressive dual performance by Oscar Isaac.

00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:04.920
"We are an unusual couple, you know."

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:06.720
"Oh, I don't think that was ever in question"

00:07:07.721 --> 00:07:12.720
WandaVision kicked off Phase 4 of the&nbsp;
MCU in early 2021; it was also the very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:17.160
first MCU TV show on Disney+. That's&nbsp;
a lot of pressure for a new series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:21.420
but WandaVision more than rose to the&nbsp;
occasion, with critics praising how smart,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:25.740
creative, and compelling the MCU&nbsp;
could be in an episodic TV format.

00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:30.240
The series begins as Wanda Maximoff and Vision&nbsp;
live out their happy lives in the small suburban&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:34.620
town of Westview, New Jersey, mere months after&nbsp;
the events of Avengers: Endgame. The only problem?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:40.320
Viz died back in Infinity War and, for some&nbsp;
reason, each episode of the show perfectly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:45.600
mimics a different era of sitcom television.&nbsp;
As the episodes go on and more light is shed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:49.980
on the mystery of what's really happening in&nbsp;
Westview, WandaVision deepens from an impeccably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.980 --> 00:07:55.140
realized homage to television to a poignant&nbsp;
and heartbreaking meditation on loss and grief.

00:07:55.800 --> 00:07:59.280
WandaVision proved that TV was a&nbsp;
worthwhile avenue for exploring MCU&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:03.240
characters who enjoyed limited screen-time&nbsp;
in the franchise's movies. It also proved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:07.440
that the format was capable of introducing new&nbsp;
fan-favorite characters, such as Kathryn Hahn's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:11.700
Agatha Harkness. The show wouldn't have&nbsp;
worked at all without Olsen and Bettany,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.700 --> 00:08:17.417
however, who give alternately hilarious,&nbsp;
moving, and devastating performances.

00:08:17.417 --> 00:08:23.520
A follow-up to 2018's lauded Black Panther, Black&nbsp;
Panther: Wakanda Forever had to walk a difficult&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:28.800
tightrope after its lead actor Chadwick Boseman,&nbsp;
who played T'Challa in multiple Phase 3 films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:33.420
died before he could reprise his role in&nbsp;
the sequel. Thankfully, the movie rises&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.420 --> 00:08:38.820
to the occasion. By having T'Challa's fate mirror&nbsp;
Boseman's, director Ryan Coogler and his co-writer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:45.000
Joe Robert Cole honor the actor, while offering&nbsp;
an avenue for fans to mourn both Boseman and his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:50.400
character. This ensures that the movie is powerful&nbsp;
and poignant, and also serves as a catalyst to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:54.840
further the stories of other leading Wakandans,&nbsp;
as each one of them move into the future.

00:08:54.840 --> 00:09:00.480
The film also includes a bevy of new and&nbsp;
exciting characters, including antagonist Namor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:05.880
leader of the underwater empire of Talokan, and&nbsp;
Riri Williams, who's poised to become Ironheart,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:10.260
the heir apparent to Iron Man. While&nbsp;
this leads to an often overstuffed story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.260 --> 00:09:14.400
in general, critics and audiences agreed&nbsp;
that Wakanda Forever is a compelling,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:19.430
emotionally satisfying installment in the&nbsp;
franchise that does right by the fallen T'Challa.

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:25.440
The first Muslim superhero in the MCU, Ms.&nbsp;
Marvel focuses on Pakistani-American teenager&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:30.360
Kamala Khan, who is granted superpowers by a&nbsp;
bangle with deep roots in her family history.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.360 --> 00:09:35.700
For many critics, Ms. Marvel stands out for how&nbsp;
breezy and charming it all feels. Before Kamala&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:41.280
develops her own powers, she's a huge Marvel fan,&nbsp;
especially of Captain Marvel, so she responds with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:45.720
surprise and a certain amount of glee when it&nbsp;
seems she's following in her hero's footsteps.

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:49.560
"Cosmic."

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:58.440
Ms. Marvel does a good job of weaving in the&nbsp;
daily rituals and expectations of a Muslim family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.440 --> 00:10:03.540
but it's less interested in presenting this&nbsp;
as social commentary than simply as a normal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:08.400
part of Kamala's life. The show isn't concerned&nbsp;
with Kamala's role as a Jersey City high school&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:13.260
student, either. Instead, the focus — and its&nbsp;
most interesting element — is Kamala's exploration&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.260 --> 00:10:18.240
of her family's history, which forces her to&nbsp;
grapple with who she is and who she wants to be.

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:22.740
Ultimately, though, the best reason&nbsp;
to watch Ms. Marvel is Iman Vellani,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:26.880
who, in her very first acting role,&nbsp;
proves to be so magnetic that it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:31.980
impossible not to enjoy her exuberant&nbsp;
performance. Vellani is a true talent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:37.423
and her bright-eyed take on Kamala Khan will bring&nbsp;
some welcome enthusiasm to future MCU projects.

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:44.040
Marvel's first holiday special, Werewolf By Night,&nbsp;
is a fascinating experiment for the MCU. Released&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.040 --> 00:10:48.600
just in time for Halloween, the atmospheric&nbsp;
one-off tells the tale of Jack Russell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:52.980
a mysterious monster hunter who joins&nbsp;
a hunt to kill a terrifying creature in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:56.880
order to win a mystical relic. Although&nbsp;
Werewolf By Night is based on the Marvel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.880 --> 00:11:01.800
comic character and considered part of the&nbsp;
MCU, the story stands entirely on its own,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:06.720
and its lack of connective tissue to the rest of&nbsp;
the saga makes it a unique entry in the franchise.

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:12.000
The special also stands out for the direction,&nbsp;
which is deftly handled by Oscar-winning composer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:16.560
Michael Giacchino, who crafts an immersive&nbsp;
black-and-white yarn that ultimately owes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:21.300
just as much to Universal's monster movies&nbsp;
of the 1930s and 1940s as it does Marvel.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.300 --> 00:11:27.120
That means Werewolf By Night is bloodier and more&nbsp;
frightening than the franchise's traditional fare,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:31.800
but it's also wryly funny and gripping — and&nbsp;
the story is all the more intriguing for its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.800 --> 00:11:36.988
open-ended conclusion, which suggests this&nbsp;
won't be the last we see of these characters.

00:11:37.110 --> 00:11:42.360
Jeremy Renner's Hawkeye debuted in 2011's Thor,&nbsp;
yet, despite being one of the original members of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:47.520
the Avengers, he has never been fleshed out as&nbsp;
much as some of his counterparts. Hawkeye aims&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:52.500
to correct this by showcasing the realities of&nbsp;
Clint's life after Avengers: Endgame, including a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:57.420
bout of hearing loss, his grief over the death&nbsp;
of his best friend, Natasha Romanoff, and his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.420 --> 00:12:01.680
love for his family, to whom he's desperately&nbsp;
trying to get back to in time for Christmas.

00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:06.840
After Hawkeye's past as the Ronin comes back&nbsp;
to haunt him, he is forced to team up with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.840 --> 00:12:12.360
his No. 1 fan, Kate Bishop. Renner plays Clint&nbsp;
as a skeptical curmudgeon who, underneath his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.360 --> 00:12:17.100
gruff exterior, cares deeply about the people he&nbsp;
loves. Kate makes for an amusing counterpoint,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.100 --> 00:12:22.560
as her overly enthusiastic desire to jump into the&nbsp;
action both frustrates and endears her to Clint.

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:27.360
The entertaining push-and-pull between Haylee&nbsp;
Steinfeld and Renner endeared critics to the show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.360 --> 00:12:32.040
too. In addition, the show offers a welcome&nbsp;
appearance by Florence Pugh's Yelena Belova,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:36.900
who improves every scene she's in,&nbsp;
as well as the surprise return of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:36.900 --> 00:12:42.300
Vincent D'Onofrio as Kingpin — marking&nbsp;
his long-awaited entry into the MCU.

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:47.580
It's long been said that the MCU suffers&nbsp;
from a lack of good villains. While there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:47.580 --> 00:12:51.480
have certainly been bright spots, the&nbsp;
franchise's bad guys have generally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:51.480 --> 00:12:55.680
had a hard time living up to the heroes.&nbsp;
Ever since the franchise began, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:55.680 --> 00:13:01.860
it has had one reliable black hat: Tom&nbsp;
Hiddleston's Loki, the god of mischief.

00:13:02.343 --> 00:13:04.083
"Surprise!"

00:13:04.083 --> 00:13:08.340
Loki has been a frequent adversary and&nbsp;
occasional ally to Thor and the Avengers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:08.340 --> 00:13:12.780
throughout the MCU's first three phases. Yet&nbsp;
while the version we knew for much of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:12.780 --> 00:13:17.820
franchise reconciled with his brother and died&nbsp;
heroically in Avengers: Infinity War, the one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:17.820 --> 00:13:22.620
who appears in Loki is a variant created when he&nbsp;
used the Tesseract to escape custody in Avengers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:22.620 --> 00:13:27.480
Endgame. Loki's new lease of life draws the&nbsp;
attention of the Time Variance Authority,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:27.480 --> 00:13:32.160
an agency of time-travelers who are&nbsp;
tasked with pruning divergent timelines.

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:37.800
This sets Loki on a trippy and delightful&nbsp;
journey across space and time, encountering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:41.640
alternative versions of himself along&nbsp;
the way. Loki really does it all:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:41.640 --> 00:13:45.780
In six episodes, the show digs even&nbsp;
further into Loki's captivating,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:45.780 --> 00:13:50.220
chaotic perspective on life, introduces&nbsp;
the Multiverse Saga's next big bad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:50.220 --> 00:13:56.117
and delivers one of the most engaging —&nbsp;
and weirdest — romances in the entire MCU.

00:13:56.160 --> 00:14:00.660
Guardians of the Galaxy director and writer&nbsp;
James Gunn has warned that there are heavy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:00.660 --> 00:14:05.580
times ahead for his ragtag band of misfit&nbsp;
superheroes in Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:05.580 --> 00:14:10.980
but before that happens, the team celebrates&nbsp;
Earth's most wonderful time of year in The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:10.980 --> 00:14:16.440
Guardians of the Galaxy Holiday Special. The story&nbsp;
primarily revolves around Mantis and Drax as they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:16.440 --> 00:14:22.080
attempt to create the perfect Christmas for Peter&nbsp;
Quill by acquiring the ultimate gift: Kevin Bacon.

00:14:22.080 --> 00:14:23.640
"Oh! I'm so excited."

00:14:24.240 --> 00:14:32.100
Mantis and Drax's fish-out-of-water antics on&nbsp;
Earth are hilarious, and it's fun to see these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:37.080
two take center stage as they attempt to figure&nbsp;
out humanity's strange customs. Things only get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:41.880
more bonkers when they finally make contact&nbsp;
with Kevin Bacon and realize he's an actor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:41.880 --> 00:14:46.800
and not the great hero Quill led them to believe.&nbsp;
The Guardians of the Galaxy Holiday Special is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:52.849
a brief but delightful Yuletide treat, sure to&nbsp;
make any MCU fan's holiday that much brighter.

00:14:52.860 --> 00:14:58.080
The MCU is known for being a live-action&nbsp;
spectacular, but the franchise got animated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:58.080 --> 00:15:03.000
when it flipped the script to ask What If...?&nbsp;
This series consists of nine stand-alone episodes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:07.920
each exploring an alternative take on the events&nbsp;
and characters of the MCU's first three phases.

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:12.900
With its lively animation, offbeat&nbsp;
characterizations, and surprising narrative turns,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:12.900 --> 00:15:17.940
What If...? is like studio-sanctioned fan&nbsp;
fiction, offering Marvel die-hards a means&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:17.940 --> 00:15:22.440
for exploring the many ways the franchise's&nbsp;
most iconic stories might have turned out.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:27.780
It's enjoyable but low-stakes viewing, and while&nbsp;
some episodes are better than others, the show's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:27.780 --> 00:15:32.884
half-hour runtime and anthology style ensure&nbsp;
that the series offers something for everyone.

00:15:32.884 --> 00:15:37.500
Shang-Chi and the Legend of the Ten Rings is&nbsp;
an origin story for the title character, who,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:37.500 --> 00:15:42.360
when the film begins, goes by the name Shaun&nbsp;
and works as a valet in San Francisco. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:42.360 --> 00:15:47.340
when Shaun is attacked on a city bus and forced&nbsp;
to defend himself, his true identity is revealed:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:47.340 --> 00:15:52.740
Shang-Chi, the wayward son of the leader of a&nbsp;
nefarious criminal organization. This triggers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:52.740 --> 00:15:57.060
a globe-trotting adventure that builds&nbsp;
to a huge showdown involving dragons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:57.060 --> 00:16:02.400
soul-eating monsters, and a fierce battle&nbsp;
between Shang-Chi and his father, Wenwu.

00:16:02.400 --> 00:16:07.260
The movie features some of the best fight&nbsp;
sequences in the MCU and a few enjoyable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:07.260 --> 00:16:11.520
nods to famous Chinese cinema genres&nbsp;
such as wuxia. Though some critics say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:11.520 --> 00:16:15.840
the movie sputters out in its second half,&nbsp;
many praised the intriguing characters and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:15.840 --> 00:16:21.337
strong performances, particularly Simu&nbsp;
Liu, who absolutely shines as Shang-Chi.

00:16:21.360 --> 00:16:27.180
Since he swung onto the big screen in Captain&nbsp;
America: Civil War, Tom Holland has been the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:27.180 --> 00:16:32.520
MCU's own Spider-Man, but Holland is actually&nbsp;
the third actor to embody the wall-crawler in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:32.520 --> 00:16:36.660
a Hollywood film. It's a situation that's&nbsp;
fairly unusual for characters in the MCU,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:36.660 --> 00:16:41.880
given its preference for less popular or more&nbsp;
rarely adapted comic-book characters. Yet the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:41.880 --> 00:16:46.260
franchise brilliantly leveraged Spider-Man's&nbsp;
place in the movie landscape with Spider-Man:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:46.260 --> 00:16:51.480
No Way Home, a film that manages to&nbsp;
move the MCU forward by looking back.

00:16:51.480 --> 00:16:56.880
The third entry in Spidey's solo series, the story&nbsp;
picks up right where the last movie left off:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:56.880 --> 00:17:01.500
with the whole world learning that Peter&nbsp;
Parker is Spider-Man. Peter goes to Doctor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:06.300
Strange in the hopes he can use magic to make&nbsp;
the world forget he has a superhero alter-ego,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:06.300 --> 00:17:09.840
but Peter interferes with the spell,&nbsp;
leading to a breach in the multiverse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:12.540
that summons several villains&nbsp;
from previous Spider-Man series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:12.540 --> 00:17:17.400
as well as Tobey Maguire and Andrew&nbsp;
Garfield's versions of Peter Parker.

00:17:17.400 --> 00:17:20.100
No Way Home is filled with fan service,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:25.740
but it never allows its adoration of previous&nbsp;
Spider-franchises to eclipse the MCU's core&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:25.740 --> 00:17:30.420
characters. The story puts Holland's Peter&nbsp;
and his friends and family front and center,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:30.420 --> 00:17:35.640
leading to a heartfelt, emotional,&nbsp;
and thoroughly gratifying MCU movie.

